            <ArticleTitle>The rabbit ear-withdrawal test: a new analgesiometric procedure.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>481-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The latency to movement of an ear exposed to radiant heat was prolonged after intravenous administration of morphine to rabbits. The quantification of this response in a relatively inactive species that is especially suited for long term and repeated tests suggests that the rabbit ear-withdrawal test will be useful for screening analgesic/anesthetic compounds.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
